  remoted: 'Remoted queue filling or discarding messages. Check agent event rate, manager CPU and the network on port 1514.',
  logs: 'grep -E " (ERROR|CRITICAL): " /var/ossec/logs/ossec.log | tail -50 and fix the reported component.',
  ports: 'Port not listening. Check the owning service (1514 remoted, 1515 authd, 55000 API) with ss -lntup and its log.',
  alertfile: 'The manager has not written alerts recently. Check that agents are connected, ossec.log for analysisd errors, and that rules are not all disabled.',
  logsize: 'The raw event archive is large (written when logall/logall_json is on). If you do not need it, set <logall>no</logall> and <logall_json>no</logall_json> in /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf and restart wazuh-manager. Otherwise cap retention: check how many days are kept with sudo ls /var/ossec/logs/archives/*/ and delete old files (dry run first: sudo find /var/ossec/logs/archives -type f -mtime +30 -print, then add -delete). Wazuh also has a log-retention option (monitord.keep_log_days in internal options) worth checking.',
  archlag: 'No raw events reached the manager recently. Check agent connectivity and logcollector, syslog sources on 514/5514, and that wazuh-remoted is running. If alerts still arrive but this is stale, confirm archives.json is still being written (logall_json).',
  archidx: 'Archives are written on disk but the newest indexed archive event is old. Check that the Filebeat archives module is enabled (archives: enabled: true in /etc/filebeat/filebeat.yml), then restart Filebeat.',
  yellow1: 'Single-node cluster: replica shards can never be assigned, so it stays yellow. Set replicas to 0: sudo curl -sk --cert /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin.pem --key /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin-key.pem -XPUT -H "Content-Type: application/json" "https://INDEXER_IP:9200/_all/_settings?expand_wildcards=all" -d \'{"index":{"number_of_replicas":0}}\' then re-check _cluster/health.',
  disc: 'On the endpoint: check the Wazuh agent service, network access to the manager on 1514, and the agent key. Remove decommissioned agents with manage_agents.',
  never: 'Enrollment never completed. Check port 1515 (authd), the registration password and the agent manager address.',
  pending: 'Agents are pending, usually just after enrollment or a manager restart. If it persists, restart the agent.',
  dash: 'On the dashboard host: systemctl status wazuh-dashboard ; journalctl -u wazuh-dashboard -n 100 ; check port 443, the TLS certificate and opensearch.hosts in /etc/wazuh-dashboard/opensearch_dashboards.yml (the indexer must be reachable).',
  dasherr: 'Review journalctl -u wazuh-dashboard for repeating errors (usually indexer connectivity or certificate problems).',
  fbtest: 'Filebeat cannot reach the indexer. Run filebeat test output, check output.elasticsearch hosts/credentials/certs in /etc/filebeat/filebeat.yml and the indexer service.',
  fberr: 'Filebeat logged errors. Run journalctl -u filebeat --since "24 hours ago" | grep -E "error| ERROR " and fix the cause (certs, credentials, connection).',
  idx: 'On the indexer host: systemctl status wazuh-indexer, review /var/log/wazuh-indexer/wazuh-cluster.log, check port 9200 and that /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin.pem is readable.',
  health: 'List problem shards: curl -k --cert admin.pem --key admin-key.pem https://IP:9200/_cluster/allocation/explain?pretty. Often caused by low disk space or a lost node.',
  disk: 'Free space now: delete old wazuh-alerts-* indices, enforce an ISM retention policy, or extend the disk. At 95% the indexer sets indices read-only.',
  ro: 'After freeing disk space, clear the block: PUT wazuh-*/_settings {"index.blocks.read_only_allow_delete": null}. Until then new alerts cannot be indexed.',
  heap: 'Raise -Xms/-Xmx in /etc/wazuh-indexer/jvm.options (equal values, max 50% of RAM and about 31 GB), then restart the indexer.',
  heapcfg: 'Set -Xms and -Xmx to the same value, no more than 50% of RAM, in /etc/wazuh-indexer/jvm.options.',
  cpu: 'Indexer CPU is saturated. Check ingestion rate and heavy queries; add CPU or nodes.',
  reject: 'Thread pools rejected requests (since restart): the indexer is overloaded. Review CPU, heap, disk I/O and shard count.',
  oom: 'The indexer hit OutOfMemoryError. Increase RAM/heap or reduce shard count and retention.',
  noalerts: 'No alerts were indexed in 24h. Check Filebeat (systemctl status filebeat ; filebeat test output), indexer health and read-only blocks.',
  lag: 'Alerts are not arriving in the indexer. Check Filebeat (systemctl status filebeat ; filebeat test output) and the indexer disk/read-only state.',
  gap: 'There were hours with zero alerts. Look for a Filebeat/indexer outage or manager restart in that window, or a silent log source.',
  volume: 'Alert volume changed sharply vs the previous 24h. Check for a stopped log source/agent group (drop) or a noisy rule/attack (spike).',
  noisy: 'One rule produces most alerts. Tune or add an exception to cut noise and indexer load.',
  load: 'High CPU load. Check top/ps for the busy process (analysisd, java, filebeat) and the event rate.',
  mem: 'Low available memory. Check which process uses it (indexer heap, dashboard) and add RAM or reduce heap.',
  swap: 'Heavy swap use hurts the indexer. Add RAM and keep swappiness low (vm.swappiness=1).',
  dsk: 'Free disk space: rotate/delete old logs and indices, or extend the volume.',
  inode: 'Inodes almost exhausted. Find directories with huge file counts (often old logs) and clean them.',
  ntp: 'Clock is not synchronised. timedatectl set-ntp true, check chronyc tracking. Time drift breaks alert timestamps and TLS.',
  oomk: 'The kernel OOM killer terminated processes. Check journalctl -k | grep -i oom, add RAM or reduce service heap.',
  failed: 'Run systemctl --failed and journalctl -u <unit> to see why these units failed.',
  maxmap: 'Set vm.max_map_count=262144 persistently (/etc/sysctl.conf) and run sysctl --system. The indexer needs it.',
  cert: 'Renew the expiring certificate with the Wazuh certificate tool and restart the affected service. An expired cert breaks Filebeat, the dashboard and the indexer.'
};

let version = 'n/a', agentSnap = null, disconnected = [], errLines = [], cnt24 = null, cntPrev = null;
let buckets = [], topRules = [], topAgents = [], highSev = 0;
let archiveAgeMin = null, alertsJsonAgeMin = null, latestAlertAge = null, managerOk = false, indexerOk = false, filebeatOk = null;
const serverRows = [];
const diskRows = []; let topIdxRows = [];

if (!hosts.size) {
  const first = [...sshFail.entries()][0];
  add('System', 'SSH connection', 'CRIT', first ? `Could not run the healthcheck over SSH (${first[1]}: ${first[0]}). No checks were possible.` : 'No SSH output received. No checks were possible.', FIX.ssh);
}
if (hosts.size) for (const [msg, n] of sshFail.entries()) add('System', `SSH connection (${n})`, 'ERROR', msg, FIX.ssh);

for (const [h, p] of hosts) {
  const k = p.k, b = p.b;
  const svc = Object.fromEntries((p.r.SVC || []).map(a => [a[0], { active: a[1], enabled: a[2], up: num(a[3]), restarts: num(a[4]) }]));
  if (k.DONE !== '1') add('System', `Script output (${h})`, 'WARN', 'The healthcheck script output was cut off, so some checks may be missing', FIX.ssh);

  // ---- system ----
  const noRoot = k.PRIV === 'none';
  if (noRoot) {
    const SEE = 'Fix the SSH user privileges (see the Privileges check).';
    const skipped = [k.MGR_PRESENT && 'Wazuh manager (daemons, config test, queues, logs, agents)', k.IDX_PRESENT && 'indexer queries (health, disk, heap, alerts)', svc.filebeat && 'Filebeat output test', 'TLS certificate expiry'].filter(Boolean);
    add('System', `Privileges (${h})`, 'ERROR', `SSH user "${k.USER}" is not root and has no passwordless sudo, so these checks were skipped: ${skipped.join('; ')}`, FIX.priv);
    if (k.MGR_PRESENT) { add('Manager', `Manager checks (${h})`, 'ERROR', 'Skipped: needs root/sudo', SEE); add('Agents', 'Agent status', 'ERROR', 'Skipped: needs root/sudo', SEE); }
    if (k.IDX_PRESENT) { add('Indexer', `Indexer checks (${h})`, 'ERROR', 'Skipped: needs root/sudo', SEE); add('Pipeline', 'Alert ingestion checks', 'ERROR', 'Skipped: needs root/sudo', SEE); }
  }
  if (!noRoot && svc['wazuh-manager'] && k.MGR_VERSION === undefined) add('Manager', `Manager checks (${h})`, 'ERROR', 'The script output has no manager section, so daemons, config test, queues and agents were not checked', 'The SSH node probably still holds an older version of the script. Re-import the latest workflow JSON or paste the new command into the SSH node.');
  if (!noRoot && svc['wazuh-manager'] && k.MGR_VERSION === undefined) add('Agents', 'Agent status', 'ERROR', 'Skipped: no manager section in the script output', 'See the Manager checks issue above.');
  const ports = new Set(); (b.PORTS || []).forEach(l => { const m = (l.split('|')[1] || '').match(/:(\d+)$/); if (m) ports.add(+m[1]); });
  if (svc['wazuh-manager']) {
    const miss = [[1514, 'agent events (remoted)', 'CRIT'], [55000, 'API', 'CRIT'], [1515, 'enrollment (authd)', 'WARN']].filter(([pt]) => !ports.has(pt));
    add('Manager', `Listening ports (${h})`, miss.length ? (miss.some(m => m[2] === 'CRIT') ? 'CRIT' : 'WARN') : 'OK', miss.length ? 'Not listening: ' + miss.map(m => `${m[0]} ${m[1]}`).join(', ') : '1514, 1515 and 55000 are listening' + (k.ESTAB_1514 !== undefined ? `; ${num(k.ESTAB_1514)} established agent TCP connection(s)` : ''), miss.length ? FIX.ports : '');
  }
  if (svc['wazuh-indexer']) add('Indexer', `Listening port 9200 (${h})`, ports.has(9200) ? 'OK' : 'CRIT', ports.has(9200) ? 'Indexer is listening on 9200' : 'Nothing is listening on 9200', ports.has(9200) ? '' : FIX.idx);
  const cpus = Math.max(1, num(k.CPUS)), load1 = num((k.LOAD || '').split(' ')[0]);
  add('System', `CPU load (${h})`, thr(load1 / cpus, cfg.load_warn_ratio, cfg.load_crit_ratio), `Load ${k.LOAD} on ${cpus} CPU(s)`, load1 / cpus >= cfg.load_warn_ratio ? FIX.load : '');
  const [mt, mu, ma] = (k.MEM_MB || '0|0|0').split('|').map(num);
  const availPct = mt ? Math.round((ma / mt) * 100) : 100;
  add('System', `Memory (${h})`, availPct < cfg.mem_crit_avail_pct ? 'CRIT' : availPct < cfg.mem_warn_avail_pct ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${Math.round(ma)} MB available of ${Math.round(mt)} MB (${availPct}%)`, availPct < cfg.mem_warn_avail_pct ? FIX.mem : '');
  const [st, su] = (k.SWAP_MB || '0|0').split('|').map(num);
  if (st > 0) add('System', `Swap (${h})`, su / st > 0.5 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${Math.round(su)} MB used of ${Math.round(st)} MB`, su / st > 0.5 ? FIX.swap : '');
  const dfs = (b.DF || []).map(l => l.split('|')).filter(a => a.length >= 4).map(a => ({ m: a[0], pct: num(a[1]), avail: num(a[2]) / 1048576, size: num(a[3]) / 1048576 }));
  if (dfs.length) {
    const w = dfs.slice().sort((x, y) => y.pct - x.pct)[0];
    const bad = dfs.filter(d => d.pct >= cfg.disk_warn_pct);
    add('System', `Disk usage (${h})`, thr(w.pct, cfg.disk_warn_pct, cfg.disk_crit_pct), bad.length ? bad.map(d => `${d.m} ${d.pct}% (${d.avail.toFixed(1)} GB free)`).join('; ') : `Highest usage ${w.pct}% on ${w.m} (${w.avail.toFixed(1)} GB free)`, bad.length ? FIX.dsk : '');
  }
  const dfi = (b.DFI || []).map(l => l.split('|')).filter(a => a.length >= 2).map(a => ({ m: a[0], pct: num(a[1]) })).sort((x, y) => y.pct - x.pct)[0];
  if (dfi) add('System', `Inodes (${h})`, thr(dfi.pct, 80, 95), `Highest inode usage ${dfi.pct}% on ${dfi.m}`, dfi.pct >= 80 ? FIX.inode : '');
  if (k.NTP === 'no') add('System', `Time sync (${h})`, 'WARN', 'System clock is not synchronised (NTP)', FIX.ntp);
  const oom = num(k.OOM24);
  add('System', `Kernel OOM kills (${h})`, oom > 0 ? 'CRIT' : 'OK', oom > 0 ? `${oom} out-of-memory kernel message(s) in the last 24h` : 'No OOM kills in the last 24h', oom > 0 ? FIX.oomk : '');
  if (k.FAILED_UNITS) add('System', `Failed systemd units (${h})`, 'WARN', k.FAILED_UNITS, FIX.failed);
  if (svc['wazuh-indexer'] && num(k.MAXMAP) && num(k.MAXMAP) < 262144) add('System', `vm.max_map_count (${h})`, 'WARN', `${k.MAXMAP} (indexer needs 262144)`, FIX.maxmap);

  const certs = (b.CERTS || []).map(l => l.split('|')).filter(a => a.length >= 3).map(a => ({ f: a[0], d: num(a[2]) })).sort((x, y) => x.d - y.d);
  if (certs.length) {
    const c0 = certs[0];
    const s = c0.d < 0 || c0.d < cfg.cert_crit_days ? 'CRIT' : c0.d < cfg.cert_warn_days ? 'WARN' : 'OK';
    const soon = certs.filter(c => c.d < cfg.cert_warn_days);
    add('System', `TLS certificates (${h})`, s, soon.length ? soon.map(c => `${c.f.split('/').slice(-3).join('/')}: ${c.d < 0 ? 'EXPIRED ' + (-c.d) + ' d ago' : c.d + ' d left'}`).join('; ') : `${certs.length} certificates, next expiry in ${c0.d} days`, s === 'OK' ? '' : FIX.cert);
  }
  const mm = Math.max(0, mt - ma);
  serverRows.push({ h, os: k.OS, up: (k.UPTIME || '').replace(/^up /, ''), load: k.LOAD, mem: `${Math.round(mu)}/${Math.round(mt)} MB`, disk: dfs.length ? Math.max(...dfs.map(d => d.pct)) + '%' : 'n/a', roles: Object.keys(svc).join(', ') });

  (b.DU || []).map(l => l.split('|')).filter(a => a.length >= 2 && a[1] !== '').forEach(a => diskRows.push({ h, p: a[0], mb: num(a[1]) }));
  if ((b.IDX_TOP || []).length) topIdxRows = b.IDX_TOP.map(l => l.trim().split(/\s+/)).filter(a => a.length >= 3).map(a => ({ i: a[0], sz: num(a[1]), docs: num(a[2]) }));

  // ---- services ----
  for (const [s, v] of Object.entries(svc)) {
    const area = s === 'wazuh-manager' ? 'Manager' : s === 'wazuh-indexer' ? 'Indexer' : s === 'wazuh-dashboard' ? 'Dashboard' : 'Pipeline';
    let status = v.active === 'active' ? 'OK' : 'CRIT';
    let det = v.active + (status === 'OK' && v.up >= 0 ? `, up ${dur(v.up)}` : '');
    if (status === 'OK' && v.restarts > 0) { status = 'WARN'; det += `, auto-restarted ${v.restarts}x by systemd (crash loop?)`; }
    if (status === 'OK' && v.enabled !== 'enabled') { status = 'WARN'; det += ', not enabled at boot'; }
    add(area, `Service ${s} (${h})`, status, det, status === 'OK' ? '' : (v.active !== 'active' && s === 'wazuh-dashboard' ? FIX.dash : FIX.svc(s)));
    if (s === 'filebeat') filebeatOk = v.active === 'active';
  }

  // ---- manager ----
  if (k.MGR_VERSION !== undefined) {
    if (k.MGR_VERSION) version = k.MGR_VERSION;
    const crit = ['wazuh-analysisd', 'wazuh-remoted', 'wazuh-db', 'wazuh-execd', 'wazuh-modulesd', 'wazuh-monitord', 'wazuh-syscheckd', 'wazuh-logcollector', 'wazuh-apid'];
    const dm = {}; (b.MGR_STATUS || []).forEach(l => { const m = l.match(/^(wazuh-\S+)\s+(is running|not running|inactive)/); if (m) dm[m[1]] = m[2] === 'is running'; });
    if (Object.keys(dm).length) {
      const down = crit.filter(x => x in dm && !dm[x]);
      const opt = Object.keys(dm).filter(x => !crit.includes(x) && !dm[x]);
      managerOk = down.length === 0;
      add('Manager', `Core daemons (${h})`, down.length ? 'CRIT' : 'OK', down.length ? 'Not running: ' + down.join(', ') : `All ${crit.length} core daemons running` + (opt.length ? ` (optional stopped: ${opt.join(', ')})` : ''), down.length ? FIX.daemons : '');
    } else add('Manager', `Core daemons (${h})`, 'ERROR', 'Could not read wazuh-control status (check root/sudo)', FIX.priv);

    const rc = num(k.CONFTEST_RC);
    const ctLines = (b.CONFTEST || []).filter(l => /ERROR|CRITICAL/.test(l)).slice(0, 2).join(' | ');
    add('Manager', `Configuration test (${h})`, rc === 0 ? 'OK' : 'CRIT', rc === 0 ? 'wazuh-analysisd -t: configuration, rules and decoders are valid' : `wazuh-analysisd -t failed (exit ${rc}): ${ctLines || (b.CONFTEST || []).slice(-2).join(' | ')}`, rc === 0 ? '' : FIX.conf);

    const an = kv(b.STATE_analysisd), rm = kv(b.STATE_remoted);
    const qs = Object.entries(an).filter(([x]) => x.endsWith('_queue_usage')).map(([x, v]) => [x, num(v)]).sort((x, y) => y[1] - x[1]);
    if (qs.length) {
      const pct = Math.round(qs[0][1] * 100);
      add('Manager', `Analysis queues (${h})`, thr(pct, cfg.queue_warn_pct, 95), `Highest queue usage ${pct}% (${qs[0][0].replace('_usage', '')})`, pct >= cfg.queue_warn_pct ? FIX.queues : '');
      const dr = num(an.events_dropped);
      add('Manager', `Events dropped (${h})`, dr > 0 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${dr.toLocaleString('en-US')} dropped, ${num(an.events_received).toLocaleString('en-US')} received, ${num(an.alerts_written).toLocaleString('en-US')} alerts written (since last restart)`, dr > 0 ? FIX.dropped : '');
    }
    if (rm.total_queue_size) {
      const qp = Math.round((num(rm.queue_size) / num(rm.total_queue_size)) * 100), disc = num(rm.discarded_count);
      add('Manager', `Remoted queue (${h})`, disc > 0 ? 'WARN' : thr(qp, cfg.queue_warn_pct, 95), `Queue ${qp}% full, ${disc} discarded, ${num(rm.tcp_sessions)} TCP sessions`, (disc > 0 || qp >= cfg.queue_warn_pct) ? FIX.remoted : '');
    }

    const nErr = num(k.LOG_ERR), nCrit = num(k.LOG_CRIT);
    errLines = (b.LOG_LAST || []).filter(Boolean);
    add('Manager', `ossec.log errors (${h})`, nCrit > 0 ? 'CRIT' : nErr > 0 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', nCrit + nErr === 0 ? 'No ERROR or CRITICAL lines in today\'s ossec.log' : `${nCrit} critical and ${nErr} error line(s) in the current ossec.log`, nCrit + nErr > 0 ? FIX.logs : '');

    if (k.ALERTS_JSON_AGE !== undefined) {
      alertsJsonAgeMin = Math.round(num(k.ALERTS_JSON_AGE) / 60);
      add('Manager', `Alert generation (${h})`, alertsJsonAgeMin > cfg.alert_file_age_min ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `alerts.json last written ${alertsJsonAgeMin} min ago`, alertsJsonAgeMin > cfg.alert_file_age_min ? FIX.alertfile : '');
    }
    if (k.ARCHIVES_PRESENT === '0') add('Pipeline', `Archives last event (${h})`, 'OK', 'Archive log (logall_json) is not enabled or not found, so there is nothing to check');
    else if (k.ARCHIVES_FILE_AGE !== undefined) {
      const fileAge = Math.round(num(k.ARCHIVES_FILE_AGE) / 60), ats = k.ARCHIVES_LAST_TS;
      const tms = ats ? Date.parse(ats.replace(/([+-]\d{2})(\d{2})$/, '$1:$2')) : NaN;
      if (!isNaN(tms)) {
        const age = Math.max(0, Math.round((Date.now() - tms) / 60000)); archiveAgeMin = age;
        const s = thr(age, cfg.archive_lag_warn_min, cfg.archive_lag_crit_min);
        add('Pipeline', `Archives last event (${h})`, s, `Last event received ${age} min ago (${ats})` + (k.ARCHIVES_LAST_AGENT ? `, from ${k.ARCHIVES_LAST_AGENT}` : '') + (k.ARCHIVES_LAST_LOC ? ` via ${k.ARCHIVES_LAST_LOC}` : ''), s === 'OK' ? '' : FIX.archlag);
      } else if (fileAge < 10) add('Pipeline', `Archives last event (${h})`, 'OK', 'Archive file was just rotated or written; no event line to read yet');
      else add('Pipeline', `Archives last event (${h})`, 'WARN', `archives.json exists but its last line has no readable timestamp (file last written ${fileAge} min ago)`, FIX.archlag);
    }
    if (k.LOGS_MB) {
      const gb = num(k.LOGS_MB) / 1024;
      add('Manager', `Wazuh log size (${h})`, gb >= cfg.logs_dir_warn_gb ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `/var/ossec/logs ${gb.toFixed(1)} GB (archives ${(num(k.ARCHIVES_MB) / 1024).toFixed(1)} GB)`, gb >= cfg.logs_dir_warn_gb ? FIX.logsize : '');
    }

    const agents = (b.AGENTS || []).map(l => { const m = l.match(/ID:\s*(\d+),\s*Name:\s*(.*?),\s*IP:\s*([^,]+),\s*(.*)$/); return m ? { id: m[1], name: m[2], ip: m[3].trim(), status: m[4].trim() } : null; }).filter(a => a && a.id !== '000');
    if (agents.length || (b.AGENTS || []).length) {
      const listOf = v => String(v || '').split(',').map(x => x.trim().toLowerCase()).filter(Boolean);
      const ign = listOf(cfg.agents_ignore), must = listOf(cfg.agents_critical);
      const ag = agents.filter(a => !ign.includes(a.name.toLowerCase()));
      const c = { active: 0, disconnected: 0, never: 0, pending: 0 };
      ag.forEach(a => { const s = a.status.toLowerCase(); if (s.startsWith('active')) c.active++; else if (s.startsWith('disconnected')) c.disconnected++; else if (s.startsWith('never')) c.never++; else if (s.startsWith('pending')) c.pending++; });
      const total = ag.length; agentSnap = { active: c.active, total };
      disconnected = ag.filter(a => a.status.toLowerCase().startsWith('disconnected'));
      const pct = total ? Math.round((c.active / total) * 1000) / 10 : 0;
      const s = !total ? 'WARN' : pct < cfg.agents_active_crit_pct ? 'CRIT' : (pct < cfg.agents_active_warn_pct || c.disconnected > 0) ? 'WARN' : 'OK';
      add('Agents', 'Connectivity', s, `${c.active}/${total} active (${pct}%), ${c.disconnected} disconnected`, s === 'OK' ? '' : FIX.disc);
      add('Agents', 'Never connected', c.never > 0 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${c.never} agent(s) never connected`, c.never > 0 ? FIX.never : '');
      add('Agents', 'Pending', c.pending > 0 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${c.pending} agent(s) pending`, c.pending > 0 ? FIX.pending : '');
      if (must.length) {
        const down = must.filter(n => { const a = agents.find(x => x.name.toLowerCase() === n); return !a || !a.status.toLowerCase().startsWith('active'); });
        add('Agents', 'Critical agents', down.length ? 'CRIT' : 'OK', down.length ? `Not active: ${down.join(', ')}` : `All ${must.length} critical agent(s) are active`, down.length ? FIX.disc : '');
      }
      if (ign.length) add('Agents', 'Ignored agents', 'OK', `${ign.length} agent name(s) excluded from the connectivity percentage (agents_ignore)`);
    } else add('Agents', 'Connectivity', 'ERROR', 'Could not read agent_control -l (check root/sudo)', FIX.priv);
  }

  // ---- filebeat ----
  if (k.FILEBEAT_TEST_RC !== undefined) {
    const rc = num(k.FILEBEAT_TEST_RC), txt = (b.FILEBEAT_TEST || []).join(' ');
    const bad = rc !== 0 || /ERR|error|fail|refused|x509/i.test(txt.replace(/errors?: ?0/gi, ''));
    add('Pipeline', `Filebeat output test (${h})`, bad ? 'CRIT' : 'OK', bad ? 'filebeat test output failed: ' + (b.FILEBEAT_TEST || []).filter(l => /ERR|error|fail|refused|x509/i.test(l)).slice(0, 2).join(' | ') : 'Filebeat can connect to the indexer (TLS and auth OK)', bad ? FIX.fbtest : '');
    const fe = num(k.FILEBEAT_ERR24);
    add('Pipeline', `Filebeat errors 24h (${h})`, fe > 20 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', fe ? `${fe} error line(s) in the last 24h` : 'No errors in the last 24h', fe > 20 ? FIX.fberr : '');
  }

  // ---- dashboard ----
  if (k.DASH_HTTP !== undefined) {
    const sc = num(k.DASH_HTTP), act = svc['wazuh-dashboard']?.active;
    let s = 'OK', d = `Dashboard answers on port ${k.DASH_PORT} (HTTP ${sc})`;
    if (sc === 0) { s = 'CRIT'; d = `Dashboard DOWN: nothing answering on port ${k.DASH_PORT}` + (act ? ` (service state: ${act})` : ''); }
    else if (sc >= 500) { s = 'CRIT'; d = `Dashboard answers with HTTP ${sc} (failing or not ready)`; }
    else if (sc >= 400 && sc !== 401 && sc !== 403) { s = 'WARN'; d = `Dashboard answers with HTTP ${sc}`; }
    add('Dashboard', `Dashboard web (${h})`, s, d, s === 'OK' ? '' : FIX.dash);
    const de = num(k.DASH_ERR24), dl = b.DASH_LAST || [];
    const lastMsg = dl.map(l => { const m = l.match(/"message":"(.*?)"(?:,|\})/); return m ? m[1] : ''; }).filter(x => x.length > 3).pop();
    const toIdx = dl.some(l => /Request Timeout|ECONNREFUSED|No Living connections|ResponseError/i.test(l));
    const dWarn = de >= cfg.dash_err_warn;
    add('Dashboard', `Dashboard log errors (${h})`, dWarn ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${de} error line(s) in the last 24h` + (de && lastMsg ? `. Latest: ${lastMsg.slice(0, 140)}` : ''), dWarn ? FIX.dasherr + (toIdx ? ' These look like dashboard-to-indexer timeouts: check indexer health, heap, CPU and disk I/O around the times in the log.' : '') : '');
  }

  // ---- indexer ----
  if (k.IDX_HTTP !== undefined) {
    const hc = jparse(b.IDX_HEALTH), idxHttp = num(k.IDX_HTTP);
    if (!hc || !hc.status) {
      const listening = ports.has(9200) && svc['wazuh-indexer']?.active === 'active';
      add('Indexer', `Indexer API (${h})`, listening ? 'ERROR' : 'CRIT',
        listening
          ? `The indexer service is active and port 9200 is listening, but the local query to ${k.IDX_URL || 'port 9200'} failed (HTTP ${idxHttp || 'no response'}). Indexer and alert checks were skipped.`
          : `Indexer not answering at ${k.IDX_URL || 'port 9200'} (HTTP ${idxHttp || 'no response'}). Indexer and alert checks were skipped.`,
        listening ? 'Check that /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin.pem and admin-key.pem exist and are valid, and that the indexer bind address matches network.host. Test by hand: sudo curl -k --cert admin.pem --key admin-key.pem https://IP:9200/_cluster/health' : FIX.idx);
    } else {
      indexerOk = hc.status === 'green';
      add('Indexer', `Cluster health (${h})`, hc.status === 'green' ? 'OK' : hc.status === 'yellow' ? 'WARN' : 'CRIT', `${String(hc.status).toUpperCase()}: ${hc.number_of_nodes} node(s), ${hc.active_shards} active shards (${Math.round(hc.active_shards_percent_as_number)}%), ${hc.unassigned_shards} unassigned, ${hc.number_of_pending_tasks} pending tasks` + ((b.IDX_UNASSIGNED || []).filter(Boolean).length ? '. e.g. ' + b.IDX_UNASSIGNED.filter(Boolean)[0].trim().slice(0, 120) : ''), hc.status === 'green' ? '' : (hc.status === 'yellow' && num(hc.number_of_nodes) === 1 ? FIX.yellow1 : FIX.health));
      const ns = jparse(b.IDX_NODES);
      if (ns && ns.nodes) for (const n of Object.values(ns.nodes)) {
        const t = n.fs?.total?.total_in_bytes, a = n.fs?.total?.available_in_bytes;
        if (t) { const used = Math.round(((t - a) / t) * 1000) / 10; const s = thr(used, cfg.disk_warn_pct, cfg.disk_crit_pct); add('Indexer', `Indexer disk (${n.name})`, s, `${used}% used, ${(a / GB).toFixed(1)} GB free of ${(t / GB).toFixed(1)} GB`, s === 'OK' ? '' : FIX.disk); }
        const heap = n.jvm?.mem?.heap_used_percent;
        if (heap !== undefined) add('Indexer', `JVM heap (${n.name})`, thr(heap, cfg.heap_warn_pct, 95), `${heap}% heap used`, heap >= cfg.heap_warn_pct ? FIX.heap : '');
        const cpu = n.os?.cpu?.percent;
        if (cpu !== undefined) add('Indexer', `Indexer CPU (${n.name})`, thr(cpu, cfg.cpu_warn_pct, 101), `${cpu}% CPU, ${n.os?.mem?.used_percent ?? '?'}% RAM`, cpu >= cfg.cpu_warn_pct ? FIX.cpu : '');
        const rej = num(n.thread_pool?.write?.rejected) + num(n.thread_pool?.search?.rejected);
        add('Indexer', `Rejected requests (${n.name})`, rej > 0 ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${rej} rejected (since restart)`, rej > 0 ? FIX.reject : '');
      }
      const bl = jparse(b.IDX_BLOCKS);
      if (bl && !bl.error) {
        const ro = Object.entries(bl).filter(([, v]) => Object.values(v?.settings || {}).some(x => String(x) === 'true')).map(([i]) => i);
        add('Indexer', 'Read-only indices', ro.length ? 'CRIT' : 'OK', ro.length ? `${ro.length} index/indices locked read-only: ${ro.slice(0, 3).join(', ')}${ro.length > 3 ? '...' : ''}` : 'No wazuh-* index is read-only', ro.length ? FIX.ro : '');
      }
      const inv = (b.IDX_INDICES || [])[0];
      if (inv && inv.includes('|')) { const [n, mn, mx, sz] = inv.split('|'); add('Indexer', 'Alert indices', 'OK', `${n} daily indices, oldest ${String(mn).slice(-10)}, newest ${String(mx).slice(-10)}, ${(num(sz) / GB).toFixed(1)} GB`); }
      const jo = (k.JVM_OPTS || '').match(/-Xms(\d+)([gGmM]).*-Xmx(\d+)([gGmM])/);
      if (jo) {
        const toMb = (v, u) => num(v) * (u.toLowerCase() === 'g' ? 1024 : 1);
        const xms = toMb(jo[1], jo[2]), xmx = toMb(jo[3], jo[4]);
        const bad = xms !== xmx || (mt && xmx > mt * 0.55);
        add('Indexer', `JVM heap settings (${h})`, bad ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `Xms ${jo[1]}${jo[2]}, Xmx ${jo[3]}${jo[4]}` + (xms !== xmx ? ' (should be equal)' : '') + (mt && xmx > mt * 0.55 ? ' (more than 50% of RAM)' : ''), bad ? FIX.heapcfg : '');
      }
      const io = num(k.IDX_OOM);
      if (io > 0) add('Indexer', `OutOfMemoryError (${h})`, 'CRIT', `${io} OutOfMemoryError line(s) in wazuh-cluster.log`, FIX.oom);

      const c1 = jparse(b.IDX_COUNT24), c0 = jparse(b.IDX_COUNTPREV);
      cnt24 = c1 && c1.count !== undefined ? c1.count : null; cntPrev = c0 && c0.count !== undefined ? c0.count : null;
      if (cnt24 === null) add('Pipeline', 'Alerts (24h)', 'ERROR', 'Could not count alerts in wazuh-alerts-*', FIX.idx);
      else add('Pipeline', 'Alerts (24h)', cnt24 > 0 ? 'OK' : 'CRIT', `${cnt24.toLocaleString('en-US')} alerts indexed in the last 24h` + (cntPrev !== null ? ` (previous 24h: ${cntPrev.toLocaleString('en-US')})` : ''), cnt24 > 0 ? '' : FIX.noalerts);
      if (cnt24 && cntPrev) {
        const chg = Math.round(((cnt24 - cntPrev) / cntPrev) * 100), bad = chg <= -cfg.volume_drop_warn_pct || chg >= cfg.volume_spike_warn_pct;
        add('Pipeline', 'Alert volume trend', bad ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `${chg > 0 ? '+' : ''}${chg}% versus the previous 24h`, bad ? FIX.volume : '');
      }
      const as = jparse(b.IDX_STATS);
      if (as && as.aggregations) {
        buckets = as.aggregations.per_hour?.buckets || [];
        topRules = (as.aggregations.top_rules?.buckets || []).map(x => ({ id: x.key, n: x.doc_count, d: x.d?.hits?.hits?.[0]?._source?.rule?.description || '' }));
        topAgents = (as.aggregations.top_agents?.buckets || []).map(x => ({ name: x.key, n: x.doc_count }));
        highSev = num(as.aggregations.high_sev?.doc_count);
        const zero = buckets.slice(0, -1).filter(x => x.doc_count === 0);
        if (cnt24 > 0) {
          const avg = cnt24 / 24, lowVol = avg < cfg.gap_min_avg_per_hour;
          const hoursTxt = zero.slice(0, 6).map(x => new Date(x.key).toISOString().slice(11, 16) + ' UTC').join(', ');
          add('Pipeline', 'Ingestion gaps', zero.length && !lowVol ? 'WARN' : 'OK', zero.length ? `${zero.length} hour(s) with zero alerts (${hoursTxt})` + (lowVol ? `. Average is only ${avg.toFixed(1)} alerts/hour, so empty hours are normal` : '') : 'Alerts arrived in every hour of the last 24h', zero.length && !lowVol ? FIX.gap : '');
        }
        if (cnt24 > 0 && topRules[0]) { const share = Math.round((topRules[0].n / cnt24) * 100); add('Pipeline', 'Noisy rule', share >= cfg.noisy_rule_pct ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `Top rule ${topRules[0].id} produces ${share}% of alerts`, share >= cfg.noisy_rule_pct ? FIX.noisy : ''); }
      }
      const ar = jparse(b.IDX_ARCH_LATEST), arts = ar?.hits?.hits?.[0]?._source?.timestamp;
      if (arts) {
        const aage = Math.round((Date.now() - Date.parse(arts.replace(/([+-]\d{2})(\d{2})$/, '$1:$2'))) / 60000);
        if (!isNaN(aage)) {
          const mismatch = aage > cfg.archive_lag_warn_min && archiveAgeMin !== null && archiveAgeMin <= cfg.archive_lag_warn_min;
          add('Pipeline', 'Archives indexed (latest)', mismatch ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `Newest indexed archive event is ${aage} min old (${arts})`, mismatch ? FIX.archidx : '');
        }
      }
      const la = jparse(b.IDX_LATEST), ts = la?.hits?.hits?.[0]?._source?.timestamp;
      if (ts) {
        const age = Math.round((Date.now() - Date.parse(ts.replace(/([+-]\d{2})(\d{2})$/, '$1:$2'))) / 60000);
        if (!isNaN(age)) {
          latestAlertAge = age;
          const lag = age > cfg.alert_lag_warn_min;
          const hint = lag ? (alertsJsonAgeMin !== null && alertsJsonAgeMin <= cfg.alert_file_age_min ? ' The manager IS writing alerts.json, so the break is between the manager and the indexer: check Filebeat first.' : '') : '';
          add('Pipeline', 'Latest alert age', lag ? 'WARN' : 'OK', `Newest indexed alert is ${age} min old (${ts})`, lag ? FIX.lag + hint : '');
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

// ===================== SUMMARY =====================
const rank = { OK: 0, WARN: 1, ERROR: 2, CRIT: 3 };
const sortRank = { CRIT: 0, ERROR: 1, WARN: 2 };
const label = { CRIT: 'CRITICAL', ERROR: 'CHECK FAILED', WARN: 'WARNING', OK: 'OK', 'N/A': 'N/A' };
const color = { OK: '#1a7f37', WARN: '#b7791f', ERROR: '#8250df', CRIT: '#cf222e', 'N/A': '#6e7781' };
const keyOf = c => c.area + '|' + c.name;
const issues = checks.filter(c => c.status !== 'OK').sort((a, b) => sortRank[a.status] - sortRank[b.status]);
const overall = checks.reduce((w, c) => (rank[c.status] > rank[w] ? c.status : w), 'OK');
const counts = { OK: 0, WARN: 0, ERROR: 0, CRIT: 0 };
checks.forEach(c => counts[c.status]++);

let sd = null; try { sd = $getWorkflowStaticData('global'); } catch (e) {}
const prevKeys = sd && Array.isArray(sd.issueKeys) ? sd.issueKeys : null;
issues.forEach(i => { i.isNew = prevKeys ? !prevKeys.includes(keyOf(i)) : false; });
const curKeys = issues.map(keyOf);
const resolved = prevKeys ? prevKeys.filter(x => !curKeys.includes(x)).map(x => x.replace('|', ' - ')) : [];
let mode = ''; try { mode = $execution.mode; } catch (e) {}
if (sd && mode === 'production') sd.issueKeys = curKeys;

const areas = ['System', 'Manager', 'Agents', 'Dashboard', 'Indexer', 'Pipeline'];
const areaStatus = a => { const cs = checks.filter(c => c.area === a); return cs.length ? cs.reduce((w, c) => (rank[c.status] > rank[w] ? c.status : w), 'OK') : 'N/A'; };
const when = $now.toFormat('yyyy-LL-dd HH:mm');
const nCrit = counts.CRIT, nWarn = counts.WARN + counts.ERROR;
const headline = overall === 'CRIT' ? `CRITICAL - ${nCrit} critical, ${nWarn} warning(s)` : overall === 'OK' ? `HEALTHY - all ${checks.length} checks passed` : `WARNINGS - ${nWarn} issue(s) to review`;
const subject = `[Wazuh Healthcheck] ${client} - ${overall === 'OK' ? 'HEALTHY' : overall === 'CRIT' ? 'CRITICAL' : 'WARNING'} - ${issues.length} issue(s) - ${when.slice(0, 10)}`;

const pill = s => `<span class="b" style="background:${color[s]}">${label[s]}</span>`;
const issueRows = issues.map(i => `<tr><td>${pill(i.status)}${i.isNew ? '<br><span class="new">NEW</span>' : ''}</td><td>${esc(i.area)}</td><td><b>${esc(i.name)}</b><br>${esc(i.detail)}</td><td class="fix">${esc(i.fix)}</td></tr>`).join('');
const compCards = areas.map(a => { const s = areaStatus(a); return `<div class="comp" style="border-top:4px solid ${color[s]}"><div class="cn">${a}</div><div class="cs" style="color:${color[s]}">${label[s]}</div></div>`; }).join('');
const snap = [['Manager', version], ['Active agents', agentSnap ? `${agentSnap.active}/${agentSnap.total}` : 'n/a'], ['Alerts 24h', cnt24 === null ? 'n/a' : cnt24.toLocaleString('en-US')], ['High severity (lvl 12+)', cnt24 === null ? 'n/a' : highSev.toLocaleString('en-US')]].map(([x, v]) => `<div class="card"><b>${esc(v)}</b>${x}</div>`).join('');
const srvRows = serverRows.map(s => `<tr><td>${esc(s.h)}</td><td>${esc(s.os)}</td><td>${esc(s.up)}</td><td>${esc(s.load)}</td><td>${esc(s.mem)}</td><td>${esc(s.disk)}</td><td>${esc(s.roles)}</td></tr>`).join('');
const disRows = disconnected.slice(0, 30).map(a => `<tr><td>${esc(a.id)}</td><td>${esc(a.name)}</td><td>${esc(a.ip)}</td></tr>`).join('');
const disMore = disconnected.length - 30;
const errRows = errLines.map(l => `<tr><td>${esc(l)}</td></tr>`).join('');
const hrs = buckets.slice(-24); const mx = Math.max(1, ...hrs.map(x => x.doc_count));
const bars = hrs.map(x => `<div class="bar" style="height:${Math.max(2, Math.round((x.doc_count / mx) * 60))}px;background:${x.doc_count === 0 ? '#cf222e' : '#2f81f7'}"></div>`).join('');
const rulesRows = topRules.map(r => `<tr><td>${esc(r.id)}</td><td>${esc(r.d)}</td><td>${r.n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td></tr>`).join('');
const agentRows = topAgents.map(r => `<tr><td>${esc(r.name)}</td><td>${r.n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td></tr>`).join('');
const allRows = checks.map(c => `<tr><td>${esc(c.area)}</td><td>${esc(c.name)}</td><td>${pill(c.status)}</td><td>${esc(c.detail)}</td></tr>`).join('');

